Fix build: DEFAULT_MLD_ALLOWED_PHY was introduced by upstream commit
07a0822e ("RDKB-62554: Provide implementation for Banana Pi STA MLO
connection (#683)") but never defined anywhere in rdk-wifi-hal or in
the rdk-wifi-libhostap headers it depends on, breaking the build with
"'DEFAULT_MLD_ALLOWED_PHY' undeclared".

wpa_supplicant's conf->mld_allowed_phy is a 3-bit band bitmap
(BIT(0)=2.4GHz, BIT(1)=5GHz, BIT(2)=6GHz; see check_mld_allowed_phy()
and wpas_sme_set_mlo_links() in wpa_supplicant/sme.c, and the
INT_RANGE(mld_allowed_phy, 0, 7) config entry in wpa_supplicant/config.c).
A value of 0 disables MLO link setup entirely (the check is used as a
boolean gate in wpas_sme_set_mlo_links()), so since this assignment
only runs when the interface actually has MLO configured
(interface->mlo_params.valid_links != 0U), the correct default is 7 -
allow MLO links on all three bands - matching the intent of the
STA MLO connection feature this line belongs to.

---
 wifi_hal_nl80211.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/wifi_hal_nl80211.c b/wifi_hal_nl80211.c
--- a/wifi_hal_nl80211.c
+++ b/wifi_hal_nl80211.c
@@ -87,6 +87,10 @@
 #define ONEWIFI_TESTSUITE_TMPFILE "/tmp/onewifi_testsuite_configured"
 #define KEY_MGMT_SAE_EXT 67108864
 #define MAX_MBSSID_INTERFACES 8
+/* Bitmap for wpa_supplicant conf->mld_allowed_phy: BIT(0)=2.4GHz,
+ * BIT(1)=5GHz, BIT(2)=6GHz (see check_mld_allowed_phy() in
+ * wpa_supplicant/sme.c). Allow MLO links on all three bands. */
+#define DEFAULT_MLD_ALLOWED_PHY 7

 #if defined(EASY_MESH_NODE) && defined(_PLATFORM_BANANAPI_R4_)
 #define CSA_TAG_ID 37
